    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 63429,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 209,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours resemble their counterparts in the uterus. Most are of spindle cell type and exhibit diffuse nuclear atypia, brisk mitotic activity, and tumour cell necrosis. Osteoclastic-like giant cells and rhabdoid cells have been reported {18777035; 20736768; 12893217}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-25T15:42:47"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
